---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqs = [["What if I skip the quarantine phase?", "You can go directly from p=none to p=reject if your aggregate reports show 100% pass rate. Quarantine is a safety net, not a requirement."], ["How do I roll back if legitimate mail is rejected?", "Lower pct= or revert to p=none. The DMARC record change propagates within minutes on Cloudflare. Then fix the failing source and re-advance."]];

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: "DMARC Enforcement Roadmap",
  description: "DMARC enforcement roadmap: p=none to p=reject in 30-60 days. Step by step with aggregate report checkpoints.",
  inLanguage: 'en',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://promptdns.com/favicon.svg' } },
  datePublished: '2026-10-27',
  dateModified: '2026-10-27',
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};

const breadcrumbs = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Email Authentication', item: 'https://promptdns.com/email-authentication/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: "DMARC Enforcement Roadmap" },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="DMARC Enforcement Roadmap: p=none to p=reject in 30-60 Days"
  description="DMARC enforcement roadmap: p=none to p=reject in 30-60 days. Step by step with aggregate report checkpoints."
  schema={[article, faqSchema, breadcrumbs]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">DMARC Enforcement Roadmap</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">DMARC Enforcement Roadmap</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-dim">DMARC enforcement roadmap: p=none to p=reject in 30-60 days with aggregate report checkpoints at each step.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class='pdns-table' style='width:100%'><thead><tr><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Phase</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Duration</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='pd-mono'>1: Monitor</td><td>Days 1-14</td><td>p=none with rua= reporting. Collect aggregate reports and identify all sources.</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>2: Fix</td><td>Days 14-21</td><td>Fix legitimate senders that fail DMARC (add include:, align return-path).</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>3: Quarantine</td><td>Days 21-35</td><td>p=quarantine with pct=25, then pct=50, then pct=100.</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>4: Reject</td><td>Days 35-60</td><td>p=reject. All legitimate sources confirmed passing.</td></tr></tbody></table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>Technical details</h2>
      <p class='mt-3'>A DMARC enforcement roadmap is a structured plan for advancing from p=none (monitoring) to p=reject (full enforcement) using aggregate report data to confirm that every legitimate sending source passes authentication before the policy is tightened.</p><p class='mt-3'>The standard timeline is 30 to 60 days: two weeks at p=none to collect baseline data, one week to fix failing legitimate senders, two weeks at p=quarantine with pct= ramping from 25 to 100, then p=reject.</p><p class='mt-3'>Advancing DMARC policy without checking aggregate reports first risks bouncing legitimate email from forgotten services such as billing systems, CRM tools, or notification platforms that send as your domain.</p>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">The step that saves the most headaches: before advancing to p=quarantine, search your aggregate reports for any source IP with more than 1% of your volume that is failing. These are almost always legitimate services someone set up without IT's knowledge.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What if I skip the quarantine phase?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">You can go directly from p=none to p=reject if your aggregate reports show 100% pass rate. Quarantine is a safety net, not a requirement.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I roll back if legitimate mail is rejected?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Lower pct= or revert to p=none. The DMARC record change propagates within minutes on Cloudflare. Then fix the failing source and re-advance.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Check your domain with our free tools:
        <a href="/spf-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SPF checker</a>,
        <a href="/dmarc-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DMARC checker</a>,
        <a href="/dkim-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DKIM checker</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
